# .gitignore — Secure Air-Gapped Platform with Integrated Guardrails
#
# This file is a CONTROL, not housekeeping. CLAUDE.md §2 invariant 4 —
# "Never commit model weights, audit logs, .env, models/, data/private/" — is
# enforced here and nowhere else in the repository. Weakening a rule below
# weakens invariant 4 directly, so treat an edit to this file the same way you
# would treat an edit to config/guardrails.yaml: deliberate, reviewed, explained.
#
# Ignoring a path reduces the risk of committing it; it does not guarantee that
# it was never committed. Anything already in git history stays in git history.
#
# NOTE ON MECHANICS: git does not descend into an ignored directory, so a
# negation such as `!models/MANIFEST.json` only works if the *directory* is not
# ignored wholesale. Where a directory has committed contents, its children are
# ignored with `dir/*` and the keepers are re-included. Do not "simplify" those
# patterns to `dir/` — that silently drops the committed files.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and derived artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never redistributed. The upstream licences, the archived-model caveat and the
# provenance rules live in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md; weights are fetched by the
# provisioning venv and verified against models/MANIFEST.json, never committed.
# `models/*` (not `models/`) so the two committed files below stay reachable.
models/*
!models/MANIFEST.json
!models/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Offline wheelhouses
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# vendor/ holds the downloaded wheels for the runtime and provisioning venvs.
# Large, platform-specific, and reconstructible from the lockfiles below.
vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audit logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audit records carry entity TYPES and COUNTS only (invariant 1), but they also
# carry hashed correlators, request IDs and timestamps that are host- and
# operator-specific. They are operational evidence, not source. Directory is
# 0700 and the JSONL files are 0600 on disk.
audit/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ingested documents and the vector store
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Under the default ingest_mode=raw (ADR-0006) the vector store holds UNMASKED
# PII at rest. It is protected by loopback binding, filesystem permissions and
# FileVault — NOT by the guardrail pipeline. None of it may reach the repo.
# Qdrant is the only vector store in this design; data/chroma/ is a defensive
# entry only, so that a stray local experiment cannot leak documents into git.
data/private/
data/qdrant/
data/chroma/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and key material
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bearer tokens (SAGP_API_TOKEN, SAGP_API_TOKEN_REVEAL), the sealed and
# provisioning environments, and any private key. .env.example is the committed
# template and carries placeholders only. The manifest signing key is
# self-signed: the public half is committed so a verifier can check the
# manifest; the private half must never be in this tree at all.
.env
.env.sealed
.env.provision
*.pem
*.key
.airgap/keys/*
!.airgap/keys/manifest_ed25519.pub
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host-specific lifecycle state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .airgap/state.json is the phase state machine (seal_generation, unseal_history)
# for one machine. Committing it would let one host's seal state be mistaken for
# another's, which is exactly the confusion the seal is meant to prevent.
.airgap/state.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evidence reports
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signed proof reports and the append-only ledger embed hostnames, paths, local
# clock timestamps and interface names. They are produced per-run and exported
# deliberately, not tracked.
evidence/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Virtualenvs, caches, build noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two venvs by design (ADR-0003): .venv is the runtime (no torch/transformers/
# huggingface-hub — invariant 10), .venv-provision is the provisioning one.
# Both are rebuilt from vendor/ + the lockfiles; neither is source.
.venv
.venv-provision
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPLICITLY KEPT — these must be committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The manifest and the lockfiles are what make the sealed build reproducible and
# verifiable. models/MANIFEST.json pins every model revision with per-file
# sha256 digests; the three lockfiles pin every wheel and artifact by hash. If
# they are not in the repo, a rebuilt environment cannot be shown to be the same
# environment, `make verify` has nothing to check the tree against, and the
# air-gap evidence loses its baseline. They are small, non-sensitive, and
# load-bearing — never ignore them, even by accident via a broader pattern.
# (These negations are also a statement of intent: if a future pattern starts
# matching one of these paths, the negation keeps the control from breaking.)
!artifacts.lock
!requirements.runtime.lock
!requirements.provision.lock
!models/MANIFEST.json
!.env.example

# docs/metrics/latest.json does not exist yet — it is produced by `make eval` at
# M6. Once produced it is the committed metrics baseline that regression gates
# compare against, so it is named here to keep it out of any future sweep.
!docs/metrics/latest.json

# Python build metadata (editable installs)
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
